      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled outpatient dose of 3,200 mg/day. A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. At this dose the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum for inflammatory conditions\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg PO four times daily or 800 mg PO twice daily\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours as needed**, for analgesia\n\nIf you do intend 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the dose you want and I'll enter it now."
      }
