      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen has no established indication, and it's well past the dose where more drug stops adding benefit and toxicity keeps climbing. That includes GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and the risk is high within a few days. I don't think I should place an order that carries that much risk of harm.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum dose)\n- Ibuprofen at a lower dose or frequency, if you tell me the indication\n- A different analgesic or anti-inflammatory regimen, if the goal is stronger effect than ibuprofen at its ceiling dose\n\nIf there's a specific clinical reason for this dose, such as a protocol or a unit I've misread, you could also talk it over with pharmacy. If the order goes through that route, it will have pharmacist review and proper documentation.\n\nTell me which option you'd like and I'll enter it."
      }
